  "description": "Nail your next time-trial or triathlon with the Vitus Auro, focused on aerodynamic efficiency to make your next ride faster\n\nThe Auro TT is packed with features to save you watts, starting with the T700 Hi-Mod UD carbon frameset with aero optimised internal cable routing and an integrated carbon aero stem and fork. The Auro also features direct mount brakes, with the rear brake integrated into the frame under the chain stays, an integrated seat clamp with aero seatpost, and an oversized BB to increase power transfer.\n\nThe Vitus Auro is the Time Trial bike of choice for the UCI Continental pro team, Vitus Pro Cycling p/b Brother UK.\n\nThe Auro TEAM eTap Disc is directly inspired by the race winning bikes of Vitus Pro Cycling. Featuring the same envy-inducing, metallic red paint job, this bike really stands out in a crowd. This race bike is fitted with SRAM’s newly launched Force eTap AXS HRD 12 speed groupset, as used on the pro team’s training bikes.\n\nThis features some industry leading technology and features; modern gearing, advanced chain management, and easy personalisation. SRAM Force eTap AXS rear derailleur capitalizes on X-Range gearing technology for enhanced range and chain management. Carbon cranks and SRAM’s new Flattop chain make this one of the most exciting new bikes in the Vitus range.\n\nThe Auro TEAM eTap comes fitted with Prime Black Edition tubeless ready carbon clincher wheels as standard. The rim depths offer the best all-round race wheels, with an 80mm rim on the rear for full aerodynamic effect, and a 65mm rim on the front to maintain positive handling in all conditions. Tyre clearance is 25mm giving you greater aero performance and comfort from the ever-reliable Continental Ultrasport II tyres.\n\nThis model is completed with a Zipp Vuka cockpit, featuring plenty of adjustment for reach and height, with Vision Metron bar end shifters, and a Vitus TT specific ‘short nose’ power saddle.",
